{
  "id": "ALAS2023-2026-3312",
  "title": "Amazon Linux 2023 - ALAS2023-2026-3312: Important priority package update for bind",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-10-26 09:00:00"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-10-26 09:00:00"
  },
  "severity": "Important",
  "description": "Package updates are available for Amazon Linux 2023 that fix the following vulnerabilities:\nCVE-2026-97313:\n\tNamed exits on an assertion failure, resulting in denial of service. Affected versions: 9.16.0-9.18.50, 9.20.0-9.20.29.\n\nCVE-2026-96888:\n\tNamed may terminate unexpectedly when a redirect zone is used with strict QNAME minimization (CWE-617). A resolver is only affected when configured with both a redirect zone AND qname-minimization strict. Affected versions: 9.16.0-9.18.50, 9.20.0-9.20.29, 9.21.0-9.21.26.\n\nCVE-2026-94300:\n\tReplaying GSS-TSIG signed UDP messages can result in memory corruption in named. An attacker who can capture a previously signed UDP message can replay it while the negotiated TSIG key is still valid. By also sending crafted queries to a zone the attacker controls, the attacker may potentially achieve remote code execution.\n\nCVE-2026-77119:\n\tA validly signed NSEC3 from an unrelated sibling zone may be accepted as an insecurity proof, downgrading a secure delegation and letting a forged unsigned answer through.\nThis issue affects BIND 9 versions 9.11.0 through 9.18.50, 9.20.0 through 9.20.27, 9.21.0 through 9.21.25, 9.11.3-S1 through 9.18.50-S1, and 9.20.9-S1 through 9.20.27-S1.\n\nCVE-2026-19668:\n\tA BIND recursive resolver may experience excessive resource consumption if it encounters large numbers of a particular kind of invalid DNSSEC record.  Default limits on \"max-records-per-type\" and \"max-types-per-name\" help mitigate the exposure.\nThis issue affects BIND 9 versions 9.11.0 through 9.18.50, 9.20.0 through 9.20.27, 9.21.0 through 9.21.25, 9.11.3-S1 through 9.18.50-S1, and 9.20.9-S1 through 9.20.27-S1.\n\nCVE-2026-19630:\n\tInbound-message resource exhaustion (CWE-400) leading to denial of service. No configuration precondition; version applicability is the deciding factor. Affected versions: 9.11.0-9.18.50, 9.20.0-9.20.29, 9.21.0-9.21.26.\n",
